# 5. WEEKLY / ALL TIME SEGMENTED CONTROL

Place a wide, pill-shaped segmented control below the header.

## Dimensions and placement

- Horizontal margin: approximately 20–24 px.
- Width: nearly the full available content width.
- Height: approximately 40 px.
- Border radius: approximately 24 px.
- Moderate vertical spacing above and below.

## Track

Use a dark purple background, approximately `#49399F`.

The track contains two equal-width segments:

1. Weekly
2. All Time

## Selected segment

By default, “Weekly” is selected.

The selected segment has:
- A lighter lavender-purple pill background.
- Fully rounded ends.
- White, semibold text.
- A subtle inset margin from the outer track.

The selected segment should occupy approximately half the width of the track.

The unselected “All Time” segment should have:
- A transparent background.
- White text at slightly reduced opacity.
- The same font size and alignment.

## Behavior

This is a real functional control, not a decorative element.

- Tapping “Weekly” displays weekly rankings.
- Tapping “All Time” displays lifetime rankings.
- The selected state updates immediately.
- Fetch or derive the appropriate ranking data using the existing backend and data model.
- Preserve the existing leaderboard functionality.
- Prevent duplicate requests from rapid taps where appropriate.
- Display an appropriate loading state without destroying the page layout.

Do not hardcode different lists solely to imitate the screenshot.

