# 8. FLOATING WHITE LEADERBOARD CONTAINER

The lower part of the screen contains a large white panel that overlaps the bottom portion of the podium.

This container holds the remaining ranked players and the current user's row when applicable.

## Container styling

- White background.
- Large rounded top corners, approximately 28–32 px.
- Rounded lower corners where the container naturally ends.
- No heavy border.
- Very soft shadow to separate it from the purple background.
- Full-width or nearly full-width within the screen.
- Horizontal margins of approximately 8–12 px.
- Positioned near the lower portion of the podium.

The container should feel like a white sheet floating over the purple background.

## Positioning

The white panel should overlap the lower section of the podium.

Use a deliberate layout strategy:
- A podium wrapper with reserved height.
- A list container that overlaps the podium wrapper by a controlled amount.
- A higher stacking order for the white list panel.

Avoid arbitrary absolute positioning that causes the podium to break on different screen sizes.

On short screens, allow vertical scrolling while preserving the intended overlap.

The panel's content must not be clipped by the screen viewport.

