# 10. SCROLLING AND RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOR

The design is primarily mobile-first.

The reference uses a narrow portrait viewport, so the layout must prioritize phone screens.

## Mobile behavior

- Keep the header visible at the top of the page.
- Keep the segmented control and highlight card in their intended positions within the page layout.
- Allow the leaderboard content to scroll vertically.
- Preserve the podium's three-column layout.
- Keep player names, flags, avatars, and scores legible.
- Prevent horizontal scrolling.
- Respect safe areas.
- Avoid overlapping the status bar or bottom navigation of the host application.

Do not shrink the entire UI proportionally to fit a short screen.

Instead, allow the page to scroll vertically when needed.

## Different screen sizes

On smaller screens:
- Reduce horizontal padding slightly.
- Reduce podium avatar size modestly if necessary.
- Allow names to wrap or truncate.
- Keep the center podium visually dominant.
- Ensure that the three platforms remain distinct.

On larger screens:
- Do not stretch every element across the full screen.
- Constrain the leaderboard to a reasonable maximum width.
- Preserve the original visual proportions.
- Center the interface where appropriate.

The page should remain visually balanced on common iOS and Android viewport sizes.

